Local changes:
- 03-woow-dotenv: the keys come from the container environment (EnvironmentFile=hermes.env), not from
  /data/options.json, and the applied-value hashes live in /opt/data/.woow-dotenv/ (root, 0700)
  because this stack has no /data. jq is not needed.
- 020-woow-provision: unchanged logic; also removes the /opt/data/ui-tui copy that 0.20.0 made.
- woow-provision: the HA s6 longrun's set_default block (webhook platform, web search/extract
  backends, browser backend) is folded in, because here hermes-provision.service runs it.
- tests: paths point at container/patches/ and tests/fixtures/; run-scoped-prompt-gc-image.py uses
  podman and needs --image (there is no published image to pin); test-approval-gate.py's usage line.

Not vendored, and why:
- patches/approval-unattended.py: HA no longer applies it; v0.22.5 routes cron/API/webhook runs to
  approvals.cron_mode / unattended_mode natively (its anchor no longer exists in tools/approval.py).
  tests/test-approval-gate.py proves the native behaviour in the built image instead.
- patches/ha-restore-ownership.py + rootfs/opt/woow/restore_ownership.py: they repair the ownership a
  Home Assistant Supervisor restore resets (it extracts addon_config as root). scripts/restore.sh
  uses podman volume export/import, which keeps the owners, and stage2 already repairs the
  hermes-owned trees, so there is nothing for it to do here.
- patches/ha-exec-boundary.py, nginx/ingress, ws_relay, cookies: Home Assistant only. The Paseo host adapter
  is vendored in phase 2 (below).

