Local changes (Paseo):
- Containerfile: HA COPYs the wrapper onto /opt/hermes/.venv/bin/hermes, which upstream ships as a
  symlink to ../../libexec/hermes; whether COPY replaces the link or writes through it depends on the
  builder. Here the link is removed and the wrapper installed in its place, and the build proves that
  upstream's /opt/hermes/bin/hermes privilege-drop shim and libexec/hermes are unchanged.
- paseo_origin.py: only the docstring and the error message (HERMES_PASEO_EXTRA_ORIGIN instead of
  paseo_ingress_url); the validation is unchanged.
- cont-init.d/04-woow-paseo-origin replaces HA's paseo_ingress_url block in 00-woow-options: it reads
  HERMES_PASEO_EXTRA_ORIGIN from the environment (hermes.env) instead of /data/options.json.
- 03-woow-dotenv also copies LITELLM_API_KEY (the Omnigent plugin's direct-execution sessions see only
  /opt/data/.env).
- 03-woow-dotenv also strips HERMES_DASHBOARD_PUBLIC_URL, HERMES_BASE_URL and HERMES_PASEO_* from
  /opt/data/.env: .env overrides the environment, so a copy there (`hermes dashboard register` writes
  one) would silently move the OAuth callback and the Paseo origin away from hermes.env.
- tests: paths point at container/; test-paseo-vendor.py checks the Podman packaging and this file;
  test-paseo-origin.py also runs every case through install.sh's hermes_origin.
